DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The system call vvmm8866() was introduced in Linux 0.97p2.  In Linux 2.1.15
       and  2.0.28,  it  was renamed to vvmm8866oolldd(), and a new vvmm8866() was intro‐
       duced.  The definition of _s_t_r_u_c_t _v_m_8_6___s_t_r_u_c_t was changed in  1.1.8  and
       1.1.9.

       These calls cause the process to enter VM86 mode (virtual‐8086 in Intel
       literature), and are used by ddoosseemmuu.

       VM86 mode is an emulation of real mode within a protected mode task.

